{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5463) from a code generation pipeline. The task is to implement `cmd/fmt` - a Go reimplementation of GNU `fmt` (text paragraph formatter) that matches the Homebrew `gfmt` reference binary. Specifically, the task requires implementing srd070 requirements R2.1 (blank line paragraph separation), R3.1 (indentation preservation), R4.1 (file and stdin input), and R5.1 (width control via -w flag). Two files must be created: `cmd/fmt/main.go` and `cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go`. The implementation must follow differential testing patterns against `gfmt`, include SIGPIPE handling, and pass all acceptance criteria.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `fmt` text paragraph reformatter reimplementation in Go\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against `gfmt`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Paragraph detection via blank lines (R2.1)\n   - Indentation preservation - first line indent preserved, subsequent lines match second line's indent (R3.1)\n   - File and stdin input handling with `-` meaning stdin (R4.1)\n   - Width control via `-w WIDTH` / `--width=WIDTH`, default 75 chars (R5.1)\n   - Goal width at 93% of width by default (R6.1)\n   - Word boundary breaking (R7.1)\n   - Space collapsing with 2 spaces after sentence-ending punctuation (R8.1)\n   - Split-only mode `-s` (R9.1), uniform spacing `-u` (R10.1), prefix mode `-p` (R11.1), tagged-paragraph mode `-t` (R12.1)\n   - Non-goals: no crown margin mode (-c), no locale-aware line breaking\n   - 40-line function size limit, 500-line file size limit\n   - Write all files before building/testing\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for fmt utility with 13 requirement groups\n     - Key requirements for this task: R2.1 (blank lines as paragraph separators), R3.1 (indentation preservation), R4.1 (file/stdin input), R5.1 (-w WIDTH flag, default 75)\n     - Additional requirements that need implementation for a functional utility: R1.1 (default formatting), R6.1 (goal width), R7.1 (word boundaries), R8.1 (space collapsing), R9.1 (split-only), R10.1 (uniform spacing), R11.1 (prefix), R12.1 (tagged paragraph), R13.1-R13.4 (exit codes and testing)\n     - Non-goals: No crown margin mode (-c), no locale-aware line breaking\n   \n   - `cmd/fmt/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Main entry point for fmt utility\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start\n     - Must implement paragraph reformatting logic\n   \n   - `cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests using `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n     - Reference binary: `gfmt` via `exec.LookPath`\n     - Must cover R2.1, R3.1, R4.1, R5.1 at minimum\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` function to be called at start of main\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary`, `NormalizeFunc`, `ComposeNormalizers`\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/build.go` (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles cmd package and returns binary path\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only one tool call was made (reading the SRD) before work was interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand all fmt requirements before planning implementation\n   - No implementation has begun yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task description with role, repository files, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constituti