hrough the logic for when to break lines based on how far the trial length overshoots the goal compared to how much the current line undershoots it—if the overshoot is greater, it's better to break and start fresh rather than keep filling. Now I'm implementing this approach in the fill function. Still writing the line-breaking logic... I'm reconsidering the `shouldBreak` approach since it actually uses both parameters meaningfully. But I'm also wondering about the `errorsastype` diagnostic—it suggests using `errors.AsType` which was added in Go 1.25, and since the project is on 1.26.3, it should be available. I'm trying to recall the exact syntax for converting an `errors.As` check into the newer `AsType` generic form, but I'm not entirely confident about how it works. The diagnostics are all suggestions rather than hard errors, but the acceptance criteria requires no warnings under golangci-lint, so I need to address both issues. Let me look at how other files in the codebase handle the `errorsastype` suggestion to understand the expected pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_read_input_tokens":72087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0ef2fe9-d254-4176-9f18-72c6679182e8","uuid":"4cde032a-a7f3-4a95-847a-1a3bb2555f5f"}
